# EAS Build treats the git repository ROOT as the project root in this
# monorepo, and (unlike a git-based checkout) copies the raw working
# directory rather than respecting .gitignore. Without this file it tries to
# package api/.venv (a 114MB Python virtualenv whose C-extension headers
# broke the upload with an ENOENT on a Windows-only file quirk) and every
# other app's node_modules, none of which the mobile build needs.
#
# Every pattern is ROOT-ANCHORED (leading slash). A bare `api/` matches a
# folder named `api` at ANY depth — including mobileapp/src/features/*/api/,
# where every feature's own API calls live — and silently dropped all of them
# from the upload, which failed a build with "Unable to resolve module
# @/features/earnings/api/earnings". Caught 2026-09-17; keep the slash.
#
# mobileapp/android is a LEFTOVER locally-generated native folder — .gitignore
# already excludes /android and /ios because this is a managed Expo project,
# but a raw-copy upload doesn't consult .gitignore. Left in, EAS finds it and
# builds from that STALE manifest instead of generating a fresh one from
# app.json — confirmed 2026-09-17: a build with this present shipped RECORD_
# AUDIO/SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW still granted and no invite Android App Link
# intent filter, both of which app.json's config plugins should have fixed.
# Excluding it forces every remote build through a clean `expo prebuild`.
#
# The rest of mobileapp/ is NOT listed here — everything else ships.
/api/
/adminWeb/
/RequirementDocs/
/mobileapp/android/
/mobileapp/ios/
